# Agent operations

Read `AGENTS.md` for project commands and conventions. `.cursor/hooks.json` wires
`preToolUse` guards for destructive shell commands, secret writes and env-file
deletes, and a `beforeReadFile` guard that keeps real env files unread. A deny means
ask the user; never rephrase a command, split it up or write through another tool
to bypass it. Real `.env` values belong to the user; commit only example templates.
Fix lint diagnostics and run the project check command before finishing.

The guards share `.claude/hooks/` with the other agent adapters. They match raw
command and write text to prevent accidents, not indirect execution or adversaries.
This adapter supplies instructions for linting and formatting; it does not install
the Claude-only TypeScript harness.
